<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dione</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dione was a Greek goddess worshipped with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> at the oracle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodona">Dodona</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, where she was his consort. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a> she is the mother of Aphrodite. Her name is a feminine form linked to that of Zeus, and she appears with him on coins of the Epirote League, reflecting the importance of Dodona as the religious centre of Epirus.</p></div>
